{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a CIBA client learns that a request has been decided (CIBA Core §5). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"push"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately absent: AXIAM does not offer it, and the FAPI-CIBA profile forbids it — push"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivers the tokens themselves to a client endpoint, which makes the notification endpoint a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token sink."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cibadeliverymode"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/ping","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/poll","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/unknown"]},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/init(rawValue:)"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/encode(to:)"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CibaDeliveryMode\/RawRepresentable-Implementations"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CibaDeliveryMode","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" is never written: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses it locally, before any request, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation failure (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P12.2, contract 1.60 A4) — never as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\""},{"type":"text","text":", never left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the server to refuse. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"ti